From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:00:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] phy: exynos5-usbdrd: release the Exynos 2200 link reset at
 exit

exynos2200_usbdrd_phy_exit() sets CLKRST_LINK_SW_RST and leaves it set,
so the DWC3 link stays in reset until the next phy_init(). But the DWC3
core touches its own registers before dwc3_core_init() calls
phy_init(): its probe reads GSNPSID and the hardware parameters, and
dwc3_phy_setup() writes the PHY configuration registers. On zuma, which
uses these ops, such an access to a link held in reset hangs the bus:
unbinding and rebinding the DWC3 freezes every CPU, with no lockup,
hung-task or sysrq panic able to reset the phone. Resume from system
suspend would hit the same path, since dwc3 exits its PHY on suspend in
device mode.

Pulse the reset instead, as exynos850_usbdrd_phy_exit() already does.
The driver zuma's stock kernel builds never leaves the link in reset
either: Google's exynos_usbcon_init_link() (exynos-usb-blkcon.c, in
phy-exynos-usbdrd-eusb-super) sets the bit, waits 10 us and clears it,
and its exit path (exynos_usbdrd_utmi_exit()) leaves the bit alone.

Tested on a Pixel 8 Pro, on the zuma-husky DT. Without this change
every rebind froze the phone (5 of 5, with and without "phy:
exynos5-usbdrd: Balance underlying UTMI PHY initialization"), and so
did 1 of 1 with the link reset kept but the PHY isolation skipped;
skipping only the link reset made the rebind work. With this change
and that commit, three unbind/bind cycles each re-enumerated the gadget
within 4 s, ssh came back each time, and dmesg showed no PHY or DWC3
error.

Fixes: cc52a697f87e ("phy: exynos5-usbdrd: support Exynos USBDRD 3.2 4nm controller")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Brett-Michael Green <brett@bmgvisualtech.com>
---
 drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos5-usbdrd.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos5-usbdrd.c b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos5-usbdrd.c
index 760b5ccb0..74b86628d 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos5-usbdrd.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-exynos5-usbdrd.c
@@ -1529,9 +1529,17 @@ static int exynos2200_usbdrd_phy_exit(struct phy *phy)
 	reg &= ~(EXYNOS2200_UTMI_FORCE_BVALID | EXYNOS2200_UTMI_FORCE_VBUSVALID);
 	writel(reg, regs_base + EXYNOS2200_DRD_UTMI);
 
+	/*
+	 * Pulse the link reset rather than leave the link in it: the DWC3
+	 * core reads its registers when it next probes, before phy_init()
+	 * runs, and on zuma such a read of a link held in reset hangs the bus.
+	 */
 	reg = readl(regs_base + EXYNOS2200_DRD_CLKRST);
 	reg |= CLKRST_LINK_SW_RST;
 	writel(reg, regs_base + EXYNOS2200_DRD_CLKRST);
+	fsleep(10);
+	reg &= ~CLKRST_LINK_SW_RST;
+	writel(reg, regs_base + EXYNOS2200_DRD_CLKRST);
 
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(phy_drd->drv_data->n_clks, phy_drd->clks);
 
